/*  EXPECTED: COMPILES and runs; compiled output must match the interpreter.

    A function wraps what it is given and stores, through that, a series it made; it is cast on a
    series of the same rabbit.

    Everything ends at the same `Done.` (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, *Open*, closed 2026-11-25). */

Bind void to work, given (the series of series of number q):
    Define t as a series of series of series of number with (q).
    Insert a series of number with (1, 2) into item 1 of t.
Done.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define mine as a series of series of number.
    Insert a series of number into mine.
    Cast work on (mine).
    State mine.
Done.
